A||||31||Archie||Dead or Alive ... WTF||||5||
Z||000000||Archie||09-18-2001||10:34 AM||||I am disappointed in the "Dead or Alive" remarks of Bush yesterday.<P>I want revenge as much as the next guy, but to kill this jerk would be ashame.<P>Our President is sworn to uphold the Constitution & The Constitution is based on laws & proper proceedure. <P>Killing this jerk would just make him a Martyr and make terriorism worse than it is.<P>We can bomb his followers to hell & it will help our cause, but We need to Arrest, try & convict this bumb and put him in prison for life. Then we hire the biggest gang in that prison to make sure he is kept alive & we need to make sure that his cellmate (Bubba) knows exactly who he is and what he has done.<P>As long as he is alive he cannot become a Martyr & others who would follow him would know what is in store for them.<P>After he is in prison and has been passed around for a while, one of the News shows needs to interview his sorry ass so that his comrads can see what we have waiting for them.<P>I'm sure that Bush was just expressing his opinion, but what he hasn't realized is that, as President, he no longer has the right to express his opinion lest it be construed as National Policy.<P>Archie <p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||09-18-2001||10:39 AM||||I agree with you in part, but don't forget, that he can be a martyr even if he's still alive and in prison.  Remember how Nelson Mandela was such a powerful figure in Africa even while he was imprisoned?  <P>This has to be handled carefully to keep bin Laden from becoming a martyr.  IMO, the best way would be for a covert wet works team to just take him out.  He's dead.  No ceremony.  No chance for last minute calls to arms.  No glory. <P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><I><FONT COLOR="blue">The path of the righteous man is beset on all sides by the inequities of the selfish and the tyrranys of evil men. Blessed is he who in the name of charity and good will shepards the weak through the valley of darkness for he is truly his brothers keeper, and the finder of lost children. And I shall strike down upon thee with great vengence and furious anger, those who attempt to poison and destroy my brothers. And you will know my name is the lord when I lay my vengence upon thee. </I></FONT></FONT><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/9-11-01a.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||09-18-2001||10:47 AM||||I agree with Archie 100%. That's not the message that needs to be sent to enhance world support.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||09-18-2001||10:48 AM||||The problem I see with imprisoning him in this country is that kooks will then be taking hostages demanding we release Bin Laden.<P>I think the "dead or alive" means more to those who would oppose bin Laden...it's obviously now easier for someone to claim a reward than it would be if were necessary Bin Laden be alive...<P>Nah...I'll take his body long before I'd want him alive...and it should be dragged through the streets of New York like those idiots dragged our servicemen through the streets of Mogadishu.||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||09-18-2001||10:55 AM||||Nah...had a better idea...<P>We take a bunch of mothballed jetliners sitting on the tarmac out in the Mojave Desert...get a bunch of out of work airline pilots to fly them to an airbase in Central Asia...strip all the seats out of the planes, fill the cargo holds with bags of ammonium nitrate, propane bottles, oxygen tanks, and a shittload of scrap metal...outfit the planes to be remotely piloted, and when bin Laden and his henchmen are captured, handcuff them to a bulkbead and crash the planes into suspected terrorist camps.<P>Of course, the planes would have the phrase "Osama Air" on the side and the face of bin Laden in a circle with a slash through it on the tail of the plane. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||09-18-2001||11:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by deceler8:<BR><B>The problem I see with imprisoning him in this country is that kooks will then be taking hostages demanding we release Bin Laden.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That could happen, however those kooks after seeing what Bin Laden looks like after Bubba gets done with him, would need to realize that once they are caught they would be in the cell right next to him.<P>To these people, the thought of being corn-holed on a regular basis would be much worse than death. This is probally one of the only images/fates that those people would fear.<P>Excuse my French.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||09-18-2001||11:08 AM||||I agree, President Bush has to be EXTEMELY careful.  I'm hoping the "Dead or Alive" was a figure of speech.<P>The age old "Take out the leader and win the war" philosopy just isn't going to work.<P>I'd rather have Bin Laden convicted and sentenced by the books rather than assasinate him.  Yea, we'd all like to see him dead, but really is killing him the "right" thing to do?  What would it accomplish?  Sure we'd all feel better, but how would the world view America?<P>I'm certain we would win more support from the rest of the world if we convict Bin Laden for his involvement in last weeks attacks, not kill him (well, death penalty after being tried would a-ok).  As for now, we need to cut economic ties, with Afganistan and any other terrist harboring country until they realize terrorism will not be accepted-tolerated and will get them nowhere.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||09-18-2001||11:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>I agree with you in part, but don't forget, that he can be a martyr even if he's still alive and in prison.  Remember how Nelson Mandela was such a powerful figure in Africa even while he was imprisoned?  <P>This has to be handled carefully to keep bin Laden from becoming a martyr.  IMO, the best way would be for a covert wet works team to just take him out.  He's dead.  No ceremony.  No chance for last minute calls to arms.  No glory. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I agree with your first statement, but the second only in part.<BR>He should be taken ALIVE and pumped for ALL info on his followers and other sects like/or associated with him in order to make a large dent in his sort/ and related beliefs!<BR>Taking him out alone will not do much good. As a matter of fact, it may make things worse around the world, but epically here in the U.S.!<BR>A surgical strike should first be done to flush those associated with him into running and exposing their location(s).<P>Archie,<BR>As to President Bushes statement, I'm not sure to take it literally as he was quoting an old wanted poster. I don't think even the top ten wanted posters say that anymore.<BR>I like the 'Bubba' idea too! Let the FBI, CIA, DOD and whoever pump him for info first!<BR>Then turn 'Bubba' loose after interviews and measurements taken first!<BR>I also think that he should be moved periodically between prisons AND trusted countries without notice and sealed hand carried communications only!<BR>Who knows what they will do to him! But the main focus should be to take him ALIVE and keep him that way, no 'special' treatment and NO RIGHTS like in Ft. Levanworth for the military prisoners. They have NO constitutional rights what so ever. Give him corn cobs to wipe his a$$ with till it just 'falls ' out of him.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever3000||09-18-2001||11:22 AM||||Although I do believe Dubya was serious, I also think it was meant as a strong message to other countries, to say he's very serious about getting this guy.  I personally would rather see him blown to pieces, or met with something really horrible.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000009||Mach10||09-18-2001||11:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>After he is in prison and has been passed around for a while, one of the News shows needs to interview his sorry ass so that his comrads can see what we have waiting for them.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Don't you mean SORE ass? &gt;:}<P>I think the best way to dispose of him would be for Bin Laden to eat some bad shellfish  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>I mean BAD shellfish. REALLY BAD shellfish  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Then US twiddles it's thumbs and says "Who Us? We'd NEVER commit such an atrocity. We send our heartfelt condolences, and condemn such an act!"<P>Then proceed to continue taking apart the rest of the Akaimo(sp?!? Only ever heard it said, never seen it in print) Network||||reg||1
Z||000010||falconhulk||09-18-2001||11:36 AM||||Bin Laden is nothing more then a bankroll.  Afganistan wants him there becasue he is proping up thier non existant economy.  This man is not a leader he is finacing to the leaders.  If he dies he dies.  The people move on.  These attacks happened before him and will happen when he is gone.  Make no mistake most of these guys target the USA becasue they think we are devils.  This nation is the most prosporus.  Why would god allow a nation who is anything other then Islamic to have such prosperity?  Their only answer is we are an afront to god.  The news would have you think these people are in such small numbers that we should not really worry.  The truth is that hundreds of their own people die in these attack on a regular basis.  If they do this to their own people what care have they for us "devils"?  I dont claim that all middle eastren people are bad.  I just cant come to grips with such a large amount of people so easily brain washed.  How do you find 19 people willing to fly themselves and a few hundred others to their death?  How do you convince people life is expendable?  Its not Osama bin laden that we must fear......its the fact that even the not so religious in these groups are willing to die to take out innocents.  How do you fight an enemy that can blend in and appears calm and normal?  How do you fight an enmy with small forces in every country in the world?  These people are not mentally ill.  You cannot pick them out of a crowd.  Nothing we do will ever satisfy them.  They will continue to wage war aginst anyone they dont agree with.  Islamic or American they dont care.  We all blow up the same.  <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Voytek||09-18-2001||12:17 PM||||Ultimately he has to die for what he did - end of story.  I know, the 'sh*t-packing-for-life' punishment sounds good but stop for a moment and do a reality check.<P>#1 - that'll never happen, and if it does, you'll never hear about it to give you the satisfaction.  The nightly news will not be reporting 'Osema Bin Laden has been sodomized again today in prison.  We have lost count of how many times this has happened.'  No, no, no.  This will never happen.  Knowing how humanitarian we all are, he'd probably be put in a special cell for his own protection.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>#2 - I agree with Decelr8 - as long as he's in prison, he stands for something and there will be more hatred and attacks.<P>Whether the US kills him right away (assassinate or otherwise) or later, he must die.  Nothing wrong with Mr. Bush's statement - it drives the message home.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Sootah||09-18-2001||12:55 PM||||God, people. I've said it once and I will say it again. Put him in a <B><I>MEXICAN</I></B> prison. Aint <I>nobody</I> wants to go to a mexican prison.<P>No, he won't be somebodys bïtch, he'll be somebodys senorìta.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">    <BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I> <BR><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter<p>[This message has been edited by Sootah (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000013||EdsB52||09-18-2001||01:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>I am disappointed in the "Dead or Alive" remarks of Bush yesterday.<P>I want revenge as much as the next guy, but to kill this jerk would be ashame.<P>Our President is sworn to uphold the Constitution & The Constitution is based on laws & proper proceedure. <P>Killing this jerk would just make him a Martyr and make terriorism worse than it is.<P>We can bomb his followers to hell & it will help our cause, but We need to Arrest, try & convict this bumb and put him in prison for life. Then we hire the biggest gang in that prison to make sure he is kept alive & we need to make sure that his cellmate (Bubba) knows exactly who he is and what he has done.<P>As long as he is alive he cannot become a Martyr & others who would follow him would know what is in store for them.<P>After he is in prison and has been passed around for a while, one of the News shows needs to interview his sorry ass so that his comrads can see what we have waiting for them.<P>I'm sure that Bush was just expressing his opinion, but what he hasn't realized is that, as President, he no longer has the right to express his opinion lest it be construed as National Policy.<P>Archie <P>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 09-18-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree that life in a US prison, eating US food would be far worse than dieing. I would hate to see Bin Laden given up dead as well, because I feel they're probably looking for a stand-in to murder and hand over right now. It's not like we have DNA on this guy, or even fingerprints. There may be US hostages taken to exchange for Bin Laden, but if the latter were dead, terrorists would find another reason to take hostages anyway. If US citizens are stupid enough to travel to adverse foreign destinations right now, they can't expect us to drop everything and rescue them. Anyone know the Lori Berenson story? She was a volunteer in Peru and supposedly linked to some terrorist group, tried in 15 minutes, and sentenced to life in the worst jail in world. She then appealed, got a new trial, and received 20 years. <P>"Our President is sworn to uphold the Constitution & The Constitution is based on laws & proper proceedure."<P>The Constitution is generally written to protect US citizens, not citizens of foreign countries. So to uphold the Constitution would not be a direct element of this situation. The President has War-Powers that kind of let him (or her) do what he wants. I do agree that it was kind of irresponsible to run off about "dead or alive," but don't think he violated the Constitution or the spirit of it in any way by that remark. The Constitution isn't really based on law, it is the law. Actually, the way I look at laws and the Constitution is that the latter gives us (US citizens) rights, while federal, state, or city laws govern, restrict, limit, or revoke those laws within their given jurisdiction. In contrast, the living Constitution, precedent, supercedes any and all written laws (statute). So it's kind of a jumbled mess, but I don't think the President is conflicting with the Constitution. <P>I believe their terrorist infrastructure includes a chain of command, and that when Bin Laden is given up/taken that someone else will take his place in some kind of context or role. We need to destroy the nucleus of their operations, up to and including the entire region.||||reg||1
Z||000014||OcalaFiero||09-18-2001||02:38 PM||||Ahhhh, Ed, it just wouldn't be a thread without your input.....||||reg||1
Z||000015||TONY_C||09-18-2001||04:14 PM||||Bin Laden will not become a martyr when the US does kill him, martyrs are a dime a dozen in places where life is considered cheap.  Look at Iran after the alloytolah(sic) died, the zealots and radicals lost all their steam, they no longer had young men volunteering to ride motorcycles thru Iraqi minefields did they?<BR>This is not about religion, I would hope every sane person would realize that no religion condones the killing of innocents or suicide for that matter. Its not about Israel or palestine either. Do you think bin laden gives a rat's ass about yassar arafat?<P>These people hate us, our friends and allies and EVERYTHING we stand for, that is to say democracy and freedom of which they cannot understand.  They want to go back in time 1000 years ago when their empire was able to keep western civilization at bay. <BR>we can't bomb them back to the stone age because they are already there. We have to make life extremely difficult for any country who harbors these barbarians.  <P>BTW, I don't see alot of people here from the NY-NJ Conn area and I live 25 miles or so from "ground zero".  on a clear day as you crest certain hills in my neighborhood on long island you could see the last ten stories or so of the towers. It's unimaginable to not be able to see them there shining in the sunlight.  I have been fortunate, yes, i say fortunate to visit the site, not too close, 8 blocks or so away.  to see the outpouring of support for the rescuers, the wall of pictures of the missing, to see otherwise tough new yorkers break down and cry is a very humbling experience. to walk thru the dust and smell the acrid smell of god knows what is still burning is something i wish every American could experience up close. <BR>I have lived in NY all my life and I always thought that someday I'd eventually get to the top of the WTC and take a look at lady Liberty looking out across the Atlantic from her spot in the harbor. Well, I missed my chance. I have already promised my kids that when the WTC towers are rebuilt, and they will certainly be, that we will be the first on line. <BR>We have to rebuild them, maybe even taller this time.  <BR>We have to win this war. <BR>We have no choice.    ||||reg||1
