Z||000021||Patrick's Dad||09-18-2001||10:27 PM||||Butter: &lt;quote&gt;We must remember this country is dealing with a MUCH different culture than our own.&lt;/quote&gt;<P>Too true. This is a people to whom dying for their belief gives them an express ride to allah. Let's give it to them. That may not be very Christian of me, but I guess that's between me and "my" God.<P>Falconhulk: &lt;quote&gt; How do you convince people life is expendable? ... How do you fight an enemy that can blend in and appears calm and normal? &lt;/quote&gt;<P>I wrote a response to this from my socially conservative POV. I thought it better not to inflame this discussion (I'm sure that I'll do it elsewhere), as we need, as a country, to remember those who gave teir lives in service to others, and, yes, avenge them.<P>We have been appointed, because of our Charter, as the police force of the planet. Sometimes we have been appointed by others, often, we appoint ourselves. When someone kills a person in my neighborhood, I expect the police to deal with them, using deadly force, if necessary. In fact, there are about three steps a police officer should utilize:<P>1) "Stop!"<P>2) "Stop, or I'll shoot!"<P>3) BANG!<P>We've sent out enough warnings. Americans died in two embassies in Africa, aboard a US ship in dock, and deep within the WTC. We're overdue for BANG!<P>BTW, the National Socialist Party of Germany were similarly indoctrinated. Hitler did not become a martyr, except to some idiots here in the US....||||reg||1
