Z||000025||RobertVol||09-19-2001||02:39 AM||||Now what we really need to do is send Bin Laden over to the UK and let him eat lots of Hamburgers and maybe get MAD COW disease   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>In all seriousness I really don't think worrying about whether he is a martyr or not is going to be crucial. I personally don't have a problem with President Bush's comments. It has been long in coming the time when we stood up in this country and said you know what? "SCREW all of you guys and your so called beliefs" The US has been there to help every major country in times of need whether it be WAR or natural disasters. Why should we really worry if another leader pops up in his place? If and when America stands up and instead of shooting a few tomahawks missiles and lets out the real "big Dogs" then you will see all this so called holy war talk cool down real quick. The real problem is they(the Middle East) do not think we will react so fiercely. I think there has been a lot of backtracking since they have seen our reaction. Well accept for the uneducated morons who think they will go to heaven for killing some infidels. Well then I think they should thank us NOW and then we can kill them all, I mean since they are going to be with Allah faster, they should be happy.... Right?<P>I really don't think we should kill innocent people, I was joking on that but I really do think they need to see we are deadly serious about this. The time about worrying about a few words the President says are over. Honestly..I am glad he is being so forward with his comments. <P>And to the comment about him being voted in office and us who voted down here in Florida,,,,, Uh I voted for President Bush and I am still glad I did. I would hate to see the other option with this going on. But even if he was I think we should support the "Office" in this time of need for our country. not the person. I would hate to be the person wearing this responsibility right now.  <BR>And when it comes to diplomatic affairs just remember ..George is listening to his staff which he picked. If I remember there is a guy named Colin Powell who know a thing or two about the middle east and what needs to be done there. And George's Dad had a staff that whipped a few butts just about a decade a go so I think he will do pretty good in this. <P>God's wisdom and speed to George W. Bush in this time of need in our country!<P><p>[This message has been edited by RobertVol (edited 09-19-2001).]||||reg||14
